            <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[.06] p-4"><strong>Proposal → QuickBooks Estimate</strong><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/60">Create or update the estimate from the CRM, then email it using QuickBooks.</p></article>
            <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[.06] p-4"><strong>Accepted proposal → invoices</strong><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/60">Create the deposit, second, or final invoice individually when Koa’s is ready to issue that milestone.</p></article>
            <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[.06] p-4"><strong>Payments remain in QuickBooks</strong><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/60">Clients pay through the QuickBooks workflow Koa’s already uses. The website never processes or records a card payment.</p></article>
            <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[.06] p-4"><strong>CRM syncs balances</strong><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-white/60">The CRM pulls invoice balance and email status from QuickBooks; the deposit reaching zero balance can complete the booking handoff.</p></article>
